Did you try giving the whole box to the robot you already trained?

Did Dusty appear because the 365 in the robot's thought bubble doesn't
match the 60?

Did you try vacuuming up the 365 and giving the box to the robot again?

When the robot finished did you see that it figured out part of the
answer?  You should have 60 times 24 in the last hole.

Do you know that you can use the robot over again after changing things
in the box?  The robot can multiply 60 times 1,440 if you change the
box just the right way.

Did you notice that the first two numbers are multiplied and the
result ends up in the last hole?

Did you try to take out the 60 and put the 1,440 in its place?

Did you put an extra zero back where the 1,440 was?

Did you replace the second 24 by the other extra zero?

Did you replace the first 24 with the 60?

Did you give the robot the box again and wait for the result?

OK, I would take the old robot and vacuum away the 365 in the box in
his thought bubble. Then I would give the box to the robot, stand
up, and leave the room so he'll finish very quickly. 
I'd sit down again and take out the 60 and put the 1,440 in its place.
Then I'd put the zero in the empty hole. I'd have the robot take out
the second 24 and put the other zero in its place.  
Then I'd take out the first 24 and put the 60 in its place. 
Then I'd give the box to the robot again. 
When he finishes the last hole of the box should have
the answer in it.
